{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_testkit_testkit", "label": "TestKit", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/testkit.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A thin convenience facade over ActorSystem for tests: quiet system, one-line probe creation, deterministic shutdown."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_testkit_testkitoptions", "label": "TestKitOptions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/testkit.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Extends ActorSystemOptionsType with quiet (default true); quiet false restores console logging while debugging a failing test."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_testkit_testkit_within", "label": "TestKit.within", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/testkit.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A soft deadline: the callback still runs to completion and the assertion throws afterwards, so it expresses an in-test SLA without depending on the runner's per-test timeout."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_testkit_testkit_shutdown", "label": "TestKit.shutdown", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/testkit.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Without it the test process leaks a live system that keeps the event loop alive - some runners detect it and fail the suite, others simply hang."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_testkit_testkit_withmanualscheduler", "label": "TestKit.withManualScheduler", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/testkit.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Returns both the kit and its ManualScheduler, with the manual scheduler wired into the system so every actor timer runs on virtual time."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_testkit_quiet_logger_default", "label": "Quiet NoopLogger default", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/testkit.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Log calls become no-ops so test output stays clean; turning logging on is an explicit opt-in for debugging."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_testkit_unique_system_names", "label": "Unique system names per test", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/testkit.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two systems with the same name on the same network would join each other once clustering is enabled, so per-test names avoid a latent identity conflict."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_testkit_testkit", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_test_probe_testprobe", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/testkit.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_testkit_testkit", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_multi_node_spec_multinodespec", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/testkit.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_testkit_testkit_withmanualscheduler", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_manual_scheduler_manualscheduler", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/testkit.